# Moonscarlet's Chat Scanner

Chat Scanner watches chat for you and alerts you only when someone posts something you are waiting for, with a sound and a clickable class-colored player name so you can whisper/invite right away.

## How I use it
I keep Trade, LFG and World in a separate chat tab, so my main tab stays clean. When I'm looking for something, I add it to the watch list and get an alert in my main tab only when it shows up.

## Features
- **Simple in-game window.** Type `/cs` or click the minimap button. No commands needed.
- **Smart keywords.** Match a word or phrase, require several words at once, or skip messages containing words you don't want (for example, find "LFM Molten Core" but skip "gold").
- **Edit anytime.** Change a keyword in place with one click.
- **Choose your chats.** Guild, Say, Yell and channels are on by default. Party, Raid, Battleground, Officer and Whispers are optional.
- **Ignore list.** Silence spammers in the scanner without touching your normal ignore list.
- **Pick your sound.** Choose the alert sound from a list and hear each one as you pick it. It can play even if game sound is muted.
- **Pick your color.** Choose the color of the alert text, with a Reset button to get the default blue back.
- **Pick your chat tab.** Send alerts to any of your chat tabs, not just the first one.
- **Raid warning style alert (optional).** Also show the match as big text in the middle of your screen.
- **Taskbar flash (optional)** when the game is in the background.
- **Class-colored, clickable player names** in every alert.
- Your own messages and repeated messages are skipped, and everything is saved between sessions.

## Getting started
1. Type `/cs` (or click the minimap button).
2. On the **Keywords** tab, type what you're looking for and press Enter.
3. Check the **Chats** tab to choose where to listen.
4. Open the **Settings** tab to choose your sound, color, chat tab and alert style, then click **Test notification** to try it.

## Keywords
| You type | It matches |
|---|---|
| `LFM Molten Core` | messages containing that phrase |
| `tank,dungeon` (commas) | messages containing **both** words |
| *Message contains:* `LFM MC` + *but NOT:* `gold,boost` | LFM MC, but not if it mentions gold or boost |

Spaces count exactly as typed, so `" tank "` only matches the whole word "tank" and not "tanked".

## Slash commands (optional)
| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `/cs` | Open or close the window |
| `/cs add [text]` | Add a keyword (`_` = space, `\|` = all must match, `-` = exclude) |
| `/cs del [number]` | Remove a keyword |
| `/cs toggle [number] [number] ...` | Turn keywords on/off (e.g. `/cs toggle 1 2 3`) |
| `/cs edit [number] [String]` | Replace a keyword (same format as add) |
| `/cs list` | Show your keywords and settings |
| `/cs clear` | Clear all keywords |
| `/cs addplayer [name]` | Ignore a player |
| `/cs delplayer [number]` | Stop ignoring a player |
| `/cs players` | Show ignored players |
| `/cs clearplayers` | Clear the ignore list |
| `/cs enable` / `/cs disable` | Turn scanning on or off |
| `/cs mute` / `/cs master` / `/cs flash` | Toggle sound / play when muted / taskbar flash |
| `/cs help` | Show all commands |